WEBVTT

00:01.160 --> 00:03.000
Is that all you've got?

00:03.000 --> 00:05.970
You've got other issues to worry
about before shard casting.

00:07.000 --> 00:08.470
That mark!

00:08.470 --> 00:12.170
That leaves us with only one choice:
to create our own place to live!

00:12.770 --> 00:14.940
I haven't been so excited in some time.

00:14.940 --> 00:17.240
Is this what they mean by "raring to go"?

00:20.120 --> 00:23.610
This is the power of shard casters...

00:24.850 --> 00:32.590
Bokutachi wa mina kitto te o nobashiterun da

00:32.590 --> 00:39.560
Tooku tooi basho e to

00:52.910 --> 00:59.120
Kaze ni fukare aruite yuku

00:59.120 --> 01:06.080
Umarekita imi o shiritakute

01:06.290 --> 01:12.600
Tatoeba ushinau toki ga kitemo

01:12.600 --> 01:19.730
Dakishimeru koto ima, erabou

01:22.180 --> 01:29.580
Bokutachi wa mina kitto te o nobashiterun da

01:29.580 --> 01:35.560
Nakusenai mono ni mukatte

01:35.560 --> 01:43.200
Kagayaita yume dake o taguriyosenagara

01:43.200 --> 01:50.070
Tooku tooi basho e to

02:06.520 --> 02:09.190
These were all acquaintances of yours,
were they not?

02:09.190 --> 02:12.890
How will you take responsibility
for their disposal?

02:12.890 --> 02:15.030
You knew?

02:15.030 --> 02:18.000
Naturally, I'll accept whatever
punishment is dealt me.

02:18.500 --> 02:21.800
But you will not be the one to deal it.

02:23.140 --> 02:26.440
I really don't care at all for your way of life.

02:27.280 --> 02:30.070
Or your very existence for that matter.

02:30.980 --> 02:33.850
I'm glad I could see your power for myself.

02:33.850 --> 02:36.650
I look forward to facing you in the Joust.

02:37.250 --> 02:38.880
Joust...

02:42.420 --> 02:45.690
Episode 4
The Wind's Resolve

02:55.040 --> 02:56.830
I don't believe it.

03:11.590 --> 03:13.190
The Joust is a competition

03:13.190 --> 03:17.060
where shard casters pit their power and
techniques against each other.

03:17.730 --> 03:22.660
Win that and you receive the title and
honor of shard champion.

03:22.660 --> 03:26.330
Teacher won that competition last year!

03:26.330 --> 03:29.470
But I'm surprised Master Robès will
be taking part in it this year.

03:29.470 --> 03:32.070
He's never entered it before.

03:32.070 --> 03:33.880
Will you enter too?

03:33.880 --> 03:36.380
Yeah, I will, and Roya will too.

03:36.380 --> 03:39.350
I've got to practice more for the competition!

03:40.550 --> 03:43.280
Man, Teacher sure is taking a while...

03:44.850 --> 03:48.810
Apparently, some Zymotan soldiers caused
a big disturbance last night.

03:49.160 --> 03:55.120
The shard champion, Dumas, has sent us a
report and apology regarding the matter.

03:56.260 --> 04:01.860
We've been raided by shard casters from other
territories a lot lately, particularly Zymotans.

04:02.340 --> 04:06.470
It is likely the result of shard-induced
damage to our protective barrier.

04:06.470 --> 04:11.780
Or they could have some joker enabling
them to do it, a spy in other words.

04:11.780 --> 04:15.980
There is also the rash of violent
spirit shard robberies.

04:15.980 --> 04:18.450
That may also be the work of the joker.

04:18.450 --> 04:22.060
We cannot overlook a possible connection
to last night's riot either.

04:22.060 --> 04:24.930
First, investigate to see if there is indeed a joker.

04:24.930 --> 04:26.490
Understood.

04:26.490 --> 04:28.500
What shall we do with Dumas?

04:28.500 --> 04:31.530
As he is the honored shard champion,

04:31.530 --> 04:34.240
I think it best that we deal with the matter
privately, to avoid scandal.

04:34.240 --> 04:36.640
I would like to hear the opinions
of you Seven Sages.

04:36.640 --> 04:39.010
By the way, Master Sebastian...

04:39.010 --> 04:43.310
I heard that you are sheltering a youth
who has come from another world.

04:43.750 --> 04:45.180
What?

04:45.180 --> 04:51.090
I'm told the boy attempted an escape after he was
apprehended on suspicion of espionage.

04:51.090 --> 04:53.590
Ah, well, that's a bit of a misunderstanding.

04:53.590 --> 04:55.420
The charges were dropped right away, you see.

04:55.420 --> 04:58.030
What about the spirit that ran amok?

04:58.030 --> 04:59.660
Umm...

04:59.660 --> 05:02.730
Is the boy a shard caster?

05:02.730 --> 05:05.300
Well, I couldn't say for sure at the moment.

05:05.300 --> 05:08.570
He is presently in Zico's care.

05:08.570 --> 05:13.770
I believe the best course is to keep
the boy there, in our hands.

05:15.440 --> 05:19.880
Elder Zico is absent yet again today.

05:19.880 --> 05:21.220
Yes...

05:21.220 --> 05:26.350
How can we trust someone who doesn't even
attend the meetings of the sages?

05:26.890 --> 05:29.560
Zico always foresees what is to come!

05:29.560 --> 05:31.230
I will not tolerate anyone speaking ill of him,

05:31.230 --> 05:33.660
even if you are a sage.

05:33.660 --> 05:35.930
Master Sebastian...

05:35.930 --> 05:38.200
Y..Yes...

05:38.200 --> 05:40.170
Philanthropy and harmony...

05:41.170 --> 05:46.510
With Templar's principles as your guide,
penetrate to the heart of this matter, Dimitri Khan.

05:46.510 --> 05:49.640
That is your duty as governor.

05:51.110 --> 05:52.410
Sir...

06:02.390 --> 06:04.060
Is this about the other day?

06:04.060 --> 06:10.570
Yes... I'm afraid that we will likely be taking back
your house and the plot of land lent to you.

06:10.570 --> 06:14.370
At the moment, we are taking care of the
various procedures and arrangements.

06:16.840 --> 06:20.310
So, then you'll be able to enter the
Joust without any punishment?

06:20.310 --> 06:21.010
That's right.

06:21.010 --> 06:22.640
Thank goodness!
That's right.

06:22.940 --> 06:27.040
Oh, speaking of that, have you heard about
the mysterious master thief, No-Face?

06:27.680 --> 06:30.220
Master thief... No-Face?

06:30.220 --> 06:32.890
They say he often appears in a flash
only to disappear just as quickly.

06:32.890 --> 06:36.620
He's always sure to leave evidence
that he committed the robbery,

06:36.620 --> 06:38.890
so that's why they call him a master thief.

06:40.560 --> 06:44.690
I heard he leaves a calling card or
these weird dolls and stuff.

06:45.500 --> 06:46.630
Weird, isn't it?

06:46.630 --> 06:48.260
Yeah, guess so.

06:48.540 --> 06:51.030
Why don't we do anything but field work?

06:52.740 --> 06:55.280
Because you need to be physically fit.

06:55.280 --> 06:57.450
You're not there yet either.

06:57.450 --> 06:59.780
Huh? Where are you going?

06:59.780 --> 07:00.250
To sleep.

07:00.250 --> 07:01.880
Huh?!
To sleep.

07:13.690 --> 07:18.730
Damn it, I want to see what kind of power I have,

07:18.730 --> 07:20.630
to see what I'm capable of!

07:57.540 --> 07:59.170
Armadole!

08:14.860 --> 08:16.460
Whoa, don't go yet!

08:16.460 --> 08:18.080
Apcarel!

08:22.460 --> 08:23.530
Why are you dodging?

08:23.530 --> 08:25.160
We can take him right down!

08:28.740 --> 08:30.200
That's it! Give him another!

08:30.200 --> 08:31.340
Run to the left!

08:31.340 --> 08:33.140
No the other way!

08:49.490 --> 08:51.330
Enough! That's enough!

08:51.330 --> 08:52.790
I give up, I give up!

08:52.790 --> 08:53.490
That will do.

08:53.490 --> 08:54.960
Apcarel!
That will do.

09:00.670 --> 09:02.530
You're too much for me, Roya.

09:03.570 --> 09:05.570
I'm no match at all.

09:05.570 --> 09:08.210
Don't talk like such a wimp before a match!

09:08.210 --> 09:09.540
Let's have another go.

09:09.540 --> 09:11.810
Forget it, let me have a little break.

09:12.680 --> 09:16.910
Oh, man, that Armadole just
doesn't do what I say.

09:30.830 --> 09:32.460
Nice breeze...

09:32.970 --> 09:34.760
I've decided.

09:36.200 --> 09:37.470
What is it?

09:37.470 --> 09:39.440
I'll enter the Joust too.

09:41.780 --> 09:43.740
I want to enter.

09:43.740 --> 09:46.780
But you can't, can you?

09:46.780 --> 09:49.650
You're not from Templar for one thing.

09:49.650 --> 09:50.650
That's right!

09:50.650 --> 09:54.560
Plus, you're violent and troublesome
and technically an ex-con.

09:54.560 --> 09:57.430
And you can't even use spirits in the first place!

09:57.430 --> 10:01.160
I... I want to put my powers to the test!

10:09.900 --> 10:11.870
You can get as worked up as you want,

10:11.870 --> 10:14.710
but if you don't have any sort of achievements,
you can't enter the Joust.

10:14.710 --> 10:16.510
Achievements?

10:46.970 --> 10:48.600
Dumas?

10:56.180 --> 10:57.810
Couldn't be.

10:58.190 --> 11:01.320
What is written here is correct, is it not?

11:01.320 --> 11:02.320
It is...

11:02.320 --> 11:06.490
In that case, we will have to ask
you to vacate the premises.

11:06.490 --> 11:10.060
You must be out no later than
one month from now.

11:10.060 --> 11:12.360
I see, very well.

11:13.900 --> 11:15.040
Teacher!

11:15.040 --> 11:17.470
There's nothing for you to worry about at all.

11:45.670 --> 11:48.930
How long do you plan to stay there like that, Zed?

11:50.910 --> 11:52.940
Why are you doing that?

11:52.940 --> 11:55.530
My patients caused a lot of trouble for everyone.

11:56.240 --> 11:58.610
This is the least I can do to atone.

11:59.410 --> 12:02.480
Not that I think this makes up for things,

12:02.480 --> 12:06.680
but by doing this, I can at least
continue to live with myself.

12:08.160 --> 12:12.320
People should live for the things they feel matter.

12:13.190 --> 12:15.160
That's what I believe.

12:20.370 --> 12:23.000
Do you really want to enter the Joust that much?

12:24.510 --> 12:26.130
I do.

13:02.740 --> 13:04.370
Stop!

13:23.460 --> 13:24.760
Him?

13:29.040 --> 13:32.700
I hereby declare the Joust open!

13:34.780 --> 13:37.780
Ah, looks like we somehow made it in time!

13:37.780 --> 13:41.280
They just finished the opening ceremony.

13:41.280 --> 13:43.080
Elder Zico!

13:43.080 --> 13:46.020
We missed you the other day.

13:46.020 --> 13:48.360
You look quite well.

13:48.360 --> 13:50.650
Yeah, I faked illness.

13:50.960 --> 13:51.960
Zico!

13:51.960 --> 13:57.230
I suppose the Council does not suit
your freedom-loving nature?

13:57.230 --> 14:00.200
You know it.

14:00.200 --> 14:07.010
You are nevertheless one of the seven sages,
and I value your opinions above all.

14:07.010 --> 14:14.380
Oh? But I would never waste the time of THE
Dimitri Khan, Templar's head of state.

14:14.380 --> 14:17.650
I hold you in the highest regard, Elder.

14:17.650 --> 14:19.750
Spare me the flattery.

14:19.750 --> 14:22.310
I mean it, Master Zico!

14:23.060 --> 14:25.890
See, only competitors are actually
allowed to enter.

14:29.760 --> 14:31.370
Ah, it's Master Zico!

14:31.370 --> 14:32.670
And Master Sebastian too!

14:32.670 --> 14:35.070
Sitting with the dignitaries, huh?
So, they're pretty important guys.

14:35.070 --> 14:37.040
It's going to start.

14:43.880 --> 14:45.480
The first match:

14:45.480 --> 14:47.950
Mickey versus Tovia!

14:50.550 --> 14:52.180
Begin!

14:58.760 --> 15:00.430
That was quick!

15:00.430 --> 15:02.050
Armadole!

15:06.100 --> 15:09.140
Whoa! I give up, I give up, I give up!

15:09.140 --> 15:11.370
The winner: Tovia!

15:12.670 --> 15:14.110
What was that all about?

15:14.110 --> 15:16.840
Mickey's not cut out to be a shard caster.

15:16.840 --> 15:19.140
He's too weak-willed and gentle.

15:20.280 --> 15:22.080
And what about you?

15:22.420 --> 15:25.650
Are you cut out for shard casting?

15:32.930 --> 15:34.550
I lost...

15:42.240 --> 15:43.840
I give up!

15:43.840 --> 15:45.810
The winner: Roya!

15:46.910 --> 15:49.840
That is your pupil, is it not?
Congratulations.

15:49.840 --> 15:51.640
Lovely, isn't she?

15:52.550 --> 15:55.480
Good luck, Master Robès!

15:55.480 --> 15:57.350
Wonderful!

16:08.600 --> 16:11.070
The winner: Robès!

16:11.070 --> 16:12.900
Way to go, Master Robès!

16:12.900 --> 16:13.670
Master Robès!

16:13.670 --> 16:16.300
Wow, he's such a hunk!
Master Robès!

16:16.540 --> 16:18.840
Master Robès!

16:21.280 --> 16:23.380
I heard about your property and all.

16:23.380 --> 16:25.780
So, that was my land, eh?

16:25.780 --> 16:29.950
I can't say it really mattered to me, but my
manservant wanted it terribly, you see.

16:29.950 --> 16:33.750
It will all be mine, the land and the
glory of the championship.

16:43.030 --> 16:44.660
Begin!

16:45.570 --> 16:48.230
What's going on, Robès?

16:54.410 --> 16:57.510
You attacked me while I was out for a stroll.

16:57.510 --> 16:59.080
I'm a victim.

16:59.080 --> 17:00.350
Why you...

17:00.350 --> 17:04.110
Or did you catch me in the middle
of something else?

17:07.550 --> 17:09.260
The winner: Dumas!

17:09.260 --> 17:11.130
You should stop taking every
little thing so seriously.

17:11.130 --> 17:13.090
It will tire you out.

17:14.400 --> 17:16.700
Zed! What should I do?

17:16.700 --> 17:19.500
Tovia said he's withdrawing
before the second round!

17:19.500 --> 17:22.700
It means I have to go out in his place!

17:22.700 --> 17:24.930
I know I can't do it!

17:27.370 --> 17:29.000
Wh..What?

17:29.310 --> 17:32.450
We will now continue with the second round!

17:32.450 --> 17:34.750
Round two, match one:

17:34.750 --> 17:36.720
Zanji versus Mickey!

17:41.990 --> 17:43.620
Begin!

17:50.730 --> 17:52.360
Zed!

18:05.710 --> 18:09.520
I... give... I give up! I give up!

18:09.520 --> 18:11.580
The winner: Mickey!

18:13.850 --> 18:15.420
Hey, is that...

18:15.420 --> 18:17.490
Take it easy.

18:17.490 --> 18:18.490
But!

18:18.490 --> 18:20.530
What are you two doing?!

18:20.530 --> 18:21.800
I... I...

18:21.800 --> 18:23.260
What's done is done.

18:23.260 --> 18:25.070
No use complaining about it now.

18:25.070 --> 18:26.400
I don't believe you!

18:26.400 --> 18:27.940
What if someone figures it out?

18:27.940 --> 18:29.570
I'll worry about that when it happens.

18:29.570 --> 18:31.040
Just keep quiet.

18:31.040 --> 18:32.340
Unbelievable...

18:34.270 --> 18:36.080
The winner: Robès!

18:36.080 --> 18:37.980
The winner: Roya!

18:37.980 --> 18:39.950
The winner: Dumas!

18:48.590 --> 18:50.560
The winner: Mickey!

18:56.830 --> 18:58.460
I give up...

18:58.900 --> 19:00.870
The winner: Arthur!

19:16.680 --> 19:18.250
Zed's amazing, isn't he?

19:18.250 --> 19:22.220
His fighting is so out of control, I can't
believe he made it to the semi-finals.

19:22.220 --> 19:24.060
He might not be able to pull
it off this time though.

19:24.060 --> 19:26.890
I mean, his opponent is the guy who beat me.

19:31.200 --> 19:31.970
What is it?

19:31.970 --> 19:33.260
Begin!
What is it?

19:36.040 --> 19:38.740
Looking away when the match has begun?

19:38.740 --> 19:40.540
He's got some nerve!

20:03.960 --> 20:05.590
It's you!

20:25.320 --> 20:27.120
St..Stop him!

20:37.200 --> 20:38.820
Stop!

20:41.570 --> 20:43.830
Who are you?

20:44.870 --> 20:47.100
Why do you come out without me calling you?

20:50.080 --> 20:52.070
What do you think you're doing?

20:53.080 --> 20:54.710
No, wait!

21:03.260 --> 21:04.660
That's him, isn't it?

21:04.660 --> 21:06.260
The boy who came from another world?

21:06.260 --> 21:08.060
That's right.

21:09.430 --> 21:11.400
It's no use with this injury.

21:11.400 --> 21:12.400
I'll withdraw.

21:12.400 --> 21:13.970
What? No way!

21:13.970 --> 21:17.440
Mr. Arthur withdrew too,
so that means Mr. Robès will win.

21:17.440 --> 21:19.440
There's nothing I can do about it.

21:19.440 --> 21:21.070
Dumas...

21:22.910 --> 21:24.210
You're not going to...

21:24.210 --> 21:28.050
Forget it, Robès is more than a match for you.

21:30.580 --> 21:32.550
A win by default?

21:32.550 --> 21:34.350
What a bore...

21:38.860 --> 21:40.260
Zed!

21:40.260 --> 21:42.230
What's going on here?

21:43.200 --> 21:45.790
I'll be fighting in Dumas's place.

21:46.330 --> 21:47.030
Oh?

21:47.030 --> 21:48.330
Hold!
Oh?

21:49.500 --> 21:52.610
You impersonate Mickey to enter the competition,

21:52.610 --> 21:56.110
throw things into complete chaos,
and now this outrage as well?!

21:56.110 --> 21:59.880
The Joust is steeped in tradition,
and I will brook no further slight against it!

21:59.880 --> 22:02.080
Withdraw from this place immediately!

22:07.450 --> 22:10.290
And what will happen if I approve of this?

22:10.660 --> 22:12.090
What?!

22:12.090 --> 22:15.320
I shall accept this match!

22:26.440 --> 22:29.100
Make this entertaining, Zed.

22:50.500 --> 22:54.370
Kimi no sono kokoro no naka o nozoite
shiritai sono kimochi to hyoujou

22:54.370 --> 22:58.270
Hitori seotta kimi no sugata kirari
hikaru namida no wake wa

22:58.270 --> 23:01.840
Kikazu ni iwazu ni okuru yo eeru
sagashiteru kotae no aida ni

23:01.840 --> 23:05.970
Kodawarisugizu kangaesugizu asu
no kimi ni komorebi kanjiru

23:07.680 --> 23:09.520
Very very much de ii kanji

23:09.520 --> 23:11.320
Very very good kimi to boku

23:11.320 --> 23:15.190
ltsudemo kimi no soba ni ite
agetai to omotterun da

23:15.190 --> 23:17.020
Very very much itsudatte

23:17.020 --> 23:18.860
Very very good kawaranai

23:18.860 --> 23:24.820
Bokura wa itsumo kibou de
chikarazuyoku saiterun da (Oh)

23:30.340 --> 23:32.810
Mayoi no naka kono yasashisa kanji

23:34.110 --> 23:36.580
Donna toki mo kimi o zutto shinji

23:37.840 --> 23:41.750
Koko ni ookiku hirogaru keshiki
buruusukai no hi no shita de

23:41.750 --> 23:45.880
li kibun ii mibun ii jibun zutto koko ni itai kibun

23:47.350 --> 23:49.160
Very very much de ii kanji

23:49.160 --> 23:50.990
Very very good kimi to boku

23:50.990 --> 23:54.800
ltsudemo kimi no soba ni ite
agetai toomotterun da

23:54.800 --> 23:56.660
Very very much itsudatte

23:56.660 --> 23:58.530
Very very good kawaranai

23:58.530 --> 24:04.490
Bokura wa itsumo kibou de
chikarazuyoku saiterun da (Oh)

24:16.250 --> 24:19.940
Next Time
The Nation of Sacred Law

24:17.350 --> 24:19.940


Next time, "The Nation of Sacred Law"
